# The .bas files are TOKENISED BASIC with a 128-byte +3DOS header, not text.
# Without this, a checkout on Windows would rewrite every 0x0A inside the
# tokenised program - and 0x0A is both a line terminator in the BASIC stream
# and an ordinary data byte - silently corrupting them and the header checksum
# with them. Marked binary so git never touches the bytes.
*.bas binary
